  "worked_solution": "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (8{t}^{3}-6{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{t}^{4}-2{t}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=-4.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =2({0}^{4})-2({0}^{3})+C \\\\ -4 & =0+C \\\\ C & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=2{t}^{4}-2{t}^{3}-4.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=3\\,\\text{s}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =2({3}^{4})-2({3}^{3})-4 \\\\  & =2(81)-2(27)-4 \\\\  & =162-54-4 \\\\  & =104\\,\\text{ft/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $104\\,\\text{ft/s}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
